mpany has received an Order-in-Original, pursuant to which the Customs Authority has imposed a redemption fine of ₹15 lakh under Section 125 of the Customs Act, 1962 and a penalty of ₹7 lakh under Section 114(iii) of the Customs Act, 1962, in relation to RoDTEP benefits claimed on certain export products. The Order, inter alia, rejects the RoDTEP claim of ₹17,01,701. iii) Date of receipt of direction or order, including any ad-interim or interim orders, or any other communication from the authority; 20.11.2026 at 09.11 a.m. iv) Details of the violation(s)/contravention(s) committed or alleged to be committed; The matter relates to RoDTEP benefits claimed by the Company in respect of certain exports of products, which were treated by the Authority as restricted export products and consequently considered ineligible for RoDTEP benefits, to the extent that the requisite Export Authorisation/NOC was not established for the relevant consignments. v) impact on financial, operation or other activities of the listed entity, quantifiable in monetary terms to the extent possible. The Company is of the view that the Order is not legally sustainable and intends to contest the same before the appropriate appellate/legal forum(s). There is no material impact on the operations or other activities of the Company. Kindly take this intimation on record. Thanking you, Yours faithfully, For SRF Limited Rajat Lakhanpal Sr. Vice President (Corporate Compliance) & Company Secretary","bodyFetched":true},{"id":"4105de7e7d68","symbol":"DIXON","company":"Dixon Technologies (India) Ltd","date":"2026-11-20","at":"2026-11-20T12:00:00.000Z","timePrecision":"day","title":"Announcement under Regulation 30 (LODR)-Analyst / Investor Meet - Outcome","subject":"Analyst / Investor Meet - Outcome","note":"Dixon held one-on-one investor meetings with Invesco and Investec on Nov 19–20, 2026; no UPSI shared.","noteSource":"screener.in","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=68d52f83