ant to Regulation 30 of the Securities and Exchange Board of India (Listing Obligations and Disclosure Requirements), Regulations, 2015. Pursuant to Regulations 30, 33 and other applicable regulations of SEBI (Listing Obligations and Disclosure Requirements), Regulations 2015 (the Listing Regulations), this is to inform you that the Board of Directors of Kaynes Technology India Limited (KTIL) at its meeting held today (i.e. November 14, 2026) have inter-alia considered and approved the following: 1. Un-audited financial results (standalone and consolidated) for the second quarter and half year ended September 30, 2026. The Un-audited financial results (standalone and consolidated) as per Indian Accounting Standards (Ind- AS) for the second quarter and half year ended September 30, 2026. A copy of the un-audited financial results along with the Limited Review Reports are enclosed herewith as Annexure A. 2. Execution of Joint Venture Agreement with Toyokawa Techno Private Limited The proposal to enter into a Joint Venture Agreement with Toyokawa Techno Private Limited for establishing a joint venture (JV) in India to undertake the business of manufacturing, assembling, testing and supplying Thin-Film Transistor Display (TFT) Modules and related products has been approved. The details of the proposed Joint Venture in accordance to the listing regulations are enclosed herewith as Annexure B. 3. Proposed voluntary strike-off of Kaynes Embedded Systems Private Limited, a subsidiary of the KTIL. The proposal for the voluntary strike-off of Kaynes Embedded Systems Private Limited (“KESPL”), a subsidiary of the KTIL in which the KTIL holds 60% of the shareholding, pursuant to Section 248(2) of the Companies Act, 2013, subject to completion of the necessary statutory formalities. The details of the proposed strike-off are enclosed herewith as Annexure C KAYNES TECHNOLOGY INDIA LIMITED CIN: L29128KA2008PLC045825 website: www.kaynestechnology.co.in email ID: kaynestechcs@kaynes