16 India Telephone No: +91 8212582595 November 14, 2026 BSE Limited Corporate Relationship Dept., 14th floor, P. J. Tower, Dalal Street, Fort Mumbai - 400 001 Scrip Code: 543664 National Stock Exchange of India Limited Exchange Plaza, Plot no. C/1, G Block, Bandra-Kurla Complex, Bandra (E), Mumbai - 400 051 Scrip Symbol: KAYNES Dear Sir/Madam, Subject: Outcome of the Board Meeting dated November 14, 2026 pursuant to Regulation 30 of the Securities and Exchange Board of India (Listing Obligations and Disclosure Requirements), Regulations, 2015. Pursuant to Regulations 30, 33 and other applicable regulations of SEBI (Listing Obligations and Disclosure Requirements), Regulations 2015 (the Listing Regulations), this is to inform you that the Board of Directors of Kaynes Technology India Limited (KTIL) at its meeting held today (i.e. November 14, 2026) have inter-alia considered and approved the following: 1. Un-audited financial results (standalone and consolidated) for the second quarter and half year ended September 30, 2026. The Un-audited financial results (standalone and consolidated) as per Indian Accounting Standards (Ind- AS) for the second quarter and half year ended September 30, 2026. A copy of the un-audited financial results along with the Limited Review Reports are enclosed herewith as Annexure A. 2. Execution of Joint Venture Agreement with Toyokawa Techno Private Limited The proposal to enter into a Joint Venture Agreement with Toyokawa Techno Private Limited for establishing a joint venture (JV) in India to undertake the business of manufacturing, assembling, testing and supplying Thin-Film Transistor Display (TFT) Modules and related products has been approved. The details of the proposed Joint Venture in accordance to the listing regulations are enclosed herewith as Annexure B. 3. Proposed voluntary strike-off of Kaynes Embedded Systems Private Limited, a subsidiary of the KTIL. The proposal for the voluntary strike-off of Kaynes Embedded Systems Private Limited (“KESPL”), a subsidiary of the KTIL in which the KTIL holds 60% of the shareholding, pursuant to Section 248(2) of the Companies Act, 2013, subject to completion of the necessary statutory formalities. The details of the proposed strike-off are enclosed herewith as Annexure C KAYNES TECHNOLOGY INDIA LIMITED CIN: L29128KA2008PLC045825 website: www.kaynestechnology.co.in email ID: kaynestechcs@kaynestechnology.net H.O & Registered office: 23-25, Belagola, Food Industrial Estate Metagalli PO, Mysore 570016 India Telephone No: +91 8212582595 The above information will also be made available on the website of the Company at www.kaynestechnology.co.in The Board Meeting commenced at 15:00 IST and concluded at 21:30 IST. We request you to kindly take the above information on record and acknowledge it. Yours faithfully, For Kaynes Technology India Limited Sudhasri Addepalli Company Secretary and Compliance Officer ICSI Membership no.: ACS 79832 Enclosed as above Walker Chandiok & Co LLP 5th Floor, No.65/2, Block “A”, Bagmane Tridib, Bagmane Tech Park, C V Raman Nagar, Bengaluru 560093 T +91 80 4243 0700 F +91 80 4126 1228 Chartered Accountants Offices in Bengaluru, Chandigarh, Chennai, Gurugram, Hyderabad, Kochi, Kolkata, Mumbai, New Delhi, Noida and Pune Walker Chandiok & Co LLP is registered with limited liability with identification number AAC-2085 and its registered office at L-41 Connaught Circus, New Delhi, 110001, India Independent Auditor’s Review Report on Standalone Unaudited Quarterly Financial Results and Year to Date Results of the Company pursuant to the Regulation 33 of the SEBI (Listing Obligations and Disclosure Requirements) Regulations, 2015 (as amended) To the Board of Directors of Kaynes Technology India Limited 1. We","bodyFetched":true,"line":"Board meeting outcome: Q2 results, the Toyokawa Techno display JV, and strike-off of a dormant subsidiary.","lineSource":"filing","orgs":["Toyokawa Techno"]},{"id":"a49105519bd8","symbol":"KAYNES","co