national Corporate Finance Mail Stop 3-9 450 Fifth Street Washington DC 20549 U.S.A. cc: Societe de la Bourse de Luxembourg 35A Boulevard Joseph II L-1840 Luxembourg","bodyFetched":true},{"id":"27c413d6c4e1","symbol":"TVSMOTOR","company":"TVS Motor Company Ltd","date":"2026-11-13","at":"2026-11-13T12:00:00.000Z","timePrecision":"day","title":"Announcement under Regulation 30 (LODR)-Change in Management","subject":"Change in Management","note":"Gaurav Gupta resigns as President, India 2W Business effective 24 Dec 2026; internal leadership changes start 20 Nov 2026.","noteSource":"screener.in","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=b463eb77-9669-42f3-920d-539fe49f910c.pdf","source":"screener/bse","category":"management_change","kind":"people","baseScore":93,"readCost":30,"rule":"subject:(appoint|cessation|resign|supera","confidence":0.9,"body":"Website: www.tvsmotor.com Email: contactus@tvsmotor.com CIN: L35921TN1992PLC022845 13th November 2026 BSE Limited Phiroze Jeejeebhoy Towers Dalal Street Mumbai 400 001 Scrip code: 532343 National Stock Exchange of India Ltd. Exchange Plaza, 5th Floor Bandra-Kurla Complex Bandra (E), Mumbai 400 051 Scrip code: TVSMOTOR Dear Sir/Madam, Sub. : Resignation of Senior Management Personnel Ref : Intimation under Regulation 30 read with Schedule III and other applicable provisions of the SEBI (Listing Obligations and Disclosure Requirements) Regulations, 2015 (“Listing Regulations”) Pursuant to Regulation 30 read with Schedule III of the Listing Regulations (as amended), it is hereby disclosed that Mr Gaurav Gupta, President – India 2W Business, a Senior Management Personnel (“SMP”) of the Company has tendered his resignation from the services of the Company with effect from the close of business hours on 24th December 2026 to pursue an external opportunity and will thereafter cease as an employee of the Company and as a member of the Senior Management effective that date. Further, the resignation letter from Mr. Gaurav Gupta is enclosed with Annexure 1. The details as required under Regulation 30 read with Schedule III of the SEBI LODR and SEBI Master Circular No. HO/49/14/14(7)2025-CFD-POD2/I/3762/2026 dated January 30, 2026 are enclosed herewith as Annexure-1. Further, we are pleased to announce the following organizational changes, effective 20th November 2026 which reflect the strength of our succession planning, the depth of our leadership pipeline and our continued commitment to empowering internal talent to lead our next phase of growth. 1. Mr. Aniruddha Haldar – Senior Vice President, People Mobility (India 2W Business) Mr. Aniruddha Haldar, currently Senior Vice President & Business Head – Commuter Mobility and Head – Corporate Brand & Media, will assume the expanded role of Senior Vice President – People Mobility (India 2W Business). 2. Mr. A Rajkumar - Senior Vice President – Business Planning Mr. A Rajkumar will continue as Senior Vice President – Business Planning and additionally assume leadership of special project in overseas business in Asian region, bringing dedicated focus, cross-functional alignment and execution discipline to this strategic programme. Website: www.tvsmotor.com Email: contactus@tvsmotor.com CIN: L35921TN1992PLC022845 3. Mr. Madhu Prakash Singh – Expanded International Business Responsibilities Mr. Madhu Prakash Singh, Vice President – International Business, will expand his responsibilities to include New Mobility Programs alongside his existing mandate to grow our international Commuter Mobility Business (CMB). 4. Mr. Sheikh Mohammed Imran – Expanded Global Retail Transformation Responsibilities Mr. Sheikh Mohammed Imran, Associate Vice President – Retail Transformation (India), will additionally lead Retail Transformation for International Business, strengthening retail capabilities and operational excellence across our global markets. Date of Occurrence of event : 13th November 2026 at 2.45 PM (IST) Thanking you, Yours truly, For T