40ae7750d8f2.pdf","source":"screener/bse","category":"press_release","kind":"order-win","baseScore":60,"readCost":10,"rule":"subject:bagging|receiving of order|order","confidence":0.9,"body":null,"bodyFetched":false},{"id":"73f5d1ec25ed","symbol":"ITC","company":"ITC Ltd","date":"2026-11-02","at":"2026-11-02T12:00:00.000Z","timePrecision":"day","title":"Announcement under Regulation 30 (LODR)-Scheme of Arrangement","subject":"Scheme of Arrangement","note":"ITC board approved merger of wholly owned subsidiary Sproutlife Foods, effective 1 April 2026, subject to approvals.","noteSource":"screener.in","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=32ee21d2-58a3-45c8-83af-c109a9bd080d.pdf","source":"screener/bse","category":"M&A","kind":"deal","baseScore":72,"readCost":26,"rule":"subject:scheme of arrangement|amalgamati","confidence":0.9,"body":"FMCG  PAPERBOARDS & PACKAGING  AGRI-BUSINESS  INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY Visit us at www.itcportal.com  Corporate Identity Number : L16005WB1910PLC001985  e-mail : enduringvalue@itc.in 2nd November, 2026 The Manager Listing Department National Stock Exchange of India Ltd. Exchange Plaza, Plot No. C-1, G Block Bandra-Kurla Complex, Bandra (East) Mumbai 400 051 The General Manager Dept. of Corporate Services BSE Ltd. P. J. Towers, Dalal Street Mumbai 400 001 Dear Sirs, Scheme of Amalgamation of Sproutlife Foods Private Limited with the Company We write to advise that the Board of Directors of the Company at the meeting held today i.e., 2nd November, 2026 has approved the Scheme of Amalgamation of Sproutlife Foods Private Limited, a wholly owned subsidiary, with the Company under Sections 230 and 232 of the Companies Act, 2013. The aforesaid Scheme of Amalgamation, which is subject to necessary approvals, will take effect from 1 st April, 2026. Enclosed please find the relevant disclosure pursuant to Regulation 30 of the SEBI (Listing Obligations and Disclosure Requirements) Regulations, 2015 read with the SEBI Master Circular dated 30 th January, 2026. The Board Meeting commenced at 2.45 p.m. and concluded at 6.05 p.m. Yours faithfully, ITC Limited (R. K. Singhi) Executive Vice President & Company Secretary Encl. as above. cc: Securities Exchange Commission Division of Corporate Finance Office of International Corporate Finance Mail Stop 3-9 450 Fifth Street Washington DC 20549 U.S.A. cc: Societe de la Bourse de Luxembourg 35A Boulevard Joseph II L-1840 Luxembourg Sl. No. Particulars Disclosures 1. Name of the entities forming part of the amalgamation / merger, details in brief such as size, turnover etc. Transferor Company - Sproutlife Foods Private Limited (‘Sproutlife’) Transferee Company - ITC Limited (‘ITC’) Details of the Transferor Company and the Transferee Company are as follows: (₹ in crores) Particulars Sproutlife ITC Total Assets 150.07 88,915.86 Turnover 451.71 80,867.49 Net Worth 5.22 68,434.16 Note: Based on Audited Standalone Financial Statements for FY 2025-26 2. Whether the transaction would fall within related party transactions? If yes, whether the same is done at “arm’s length” Sproutlife, being a wholly owned subsidiary, is a related party of ITC. Transfer of all assets, liabilities, rights, obligations and employees of Sproutlife to ITC, as part of the proposal for amalgamation, will be at arm’s length. 3. Area of business of the entities Transferor Company: Sproutlife is primarily engaged in the business of manufacture and sale of food products, including bars, muesli, oats, protein-rich foods and peanut butter, catering to health-conscious consumers under the new-age, digital-first brand ‘Yoga Bar’. Transferee Company: ITC is one of India’s leading private sector companies and a diversified conglomerate with businesses spanning Fast Moving Consumer Goods (Cigarettes & Cigars, Branded Packaged Foods, Personal Care Products, Education & Stationery Products, Safety Matches and Agarbattis), Paperboards, Paper and Packaging, and Agri Business. 4. Rationale for amalgamation / merger The proposed amalgamation of Sproutlife with ITC will, inter alia, have the following benefits: (a) Enable seamless integration of business operations of both the companies, thereby unlocking the full potential of the combined business operations and maximising value creation opportunities through realisation of synergies; (b) Achieve optimal deployment of financial, managerial and operational resources across the combined business operations by accessing the shared talent pool and common resources; (c) Enhance efficiency of capital allocation by consolidating and optimising the cash flows and financial resources of both the companies; and (d) Result in reduction of the number of operating entities to simplify the corporate holding structure. Sl. No. Particulars Disclosures 5. In case of cash consideration - amount or otherwise sh","bodyFetched":true},{"id":"7c249072a614","symbol":"ITC","company":"ITC Ltd","date":"2026-11-02","at":"2026-11-02T12:00:00.000Z","timePrecision":"day","title":"Unaudited Financial Results - Media Statement And Presentation","subject":"Unaudited Financial Results - Media Statement And Presentation","note":"ITC announced Q2 FY27 unaudited results, with 19% revenue growth and segment updates.","noteSource":"screener.in","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=ff62231c-b3bd-48d1-a643-8b379a46cb57.pdf","source":"screener/bse","category":"results","kind":"results-deck","baseScore":42,"readCost":28,"rule":"subject:investor presentation|results pr","confidence":0.9,"body":null,"bodyFetched":false},{"id":"7bf6b29785c3","symbol":"ITC","company":"ITC Ltd","date":"2026-11-02","at":"2026-11-02T12:00:00.000Z","timePrecision":"day","title":"Unaudited Financial Results Of The Company For The Quarter And Six Months Ended 30Th September, 2026","subject":"Unaudited Financial Results Of The Company For The Quarter And Six Months Ended 30Th September, 2026","note":"ITC Q2 FY27 results approved; Sproutlife amalgamation and Century Pulp acquisition disclosed.","noteSource":"screener.in","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=6ad82347-ac2d-4385-ae80-3cd07c428f69.pdf","source":"screener/bse","category":"results","kind":"results","baseScore":78,"readCost":28,"rule":"subject:financial results?|results? for ","confidence":0.9,"body":null,"bodyFetched":false,"results":{"period":"Sep 2026","periodKey":"2026-09-30","prevPeriod":"Jun 2026","yagoPeriod":"Sep 2025","isFinancial":false,"rows":[{"key":"revenue","label":"Revenue","value":20269,"qoq":6,"yoy":3.9,"prev":19114,"yago":19502},{"key":"ebitda","label":"EBITDA","value":5645,"qoq":9,"yoy":-15.7,"prev":5181,"yago":6695},{"key":"pbt","label":"PBT","value":5695,"qoq":-2.8,"yoy":-18.4,"prev":5861,"yago":6979},{"key":"pat","label":"PAT","value":4229,"qoq":-6.2,"yoy":-18.5,"prev":4509,"yago":5187}],"margins":{"ebitda":{"cur":27.9,"prev":27.1,"yago":34.3},"pat":{"cur":20.9,"prev":23.6,"yago":26.6}},"otherIncomeShareOfPbt":10.2,"sourcePdf":"https://www.screener.in/company/source/quarter/1552/9/2026/","source":"https://www.screener.in/company/ITC/consolidated/#quarters"},"resultsPending":null},{"id":"000b7659ab3c","symbol":"MUTHOOTFIN","company":"Muthoot Finance Ltd","date":"2026-11-02","at":"2026-11-02T12:00:00.000Z","timePrecision":"day","title":"Search Under The Provisions Section 67 Of CGST Act, 2017","subject":"Search Under The Provisions Section 67 Of CGST Act, 2017","note":"GST Department conducted search at registered office on Oct 29-30, 2026; business operations continued unaffected.","noteSource":"screener.in","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=3c0dc1db-ee35-4dc0-969a-8d9d547005f9.pdf","source":"screener/bse","category":"litigation","kind":"regulatory","baseScore":65,"readCost":22,"rule":"subject:(show cause|penalt|\\bfines?\\b|ad","confidence":0.9,"body":"Ref: SEC/MFL/SE/2026/6794 November 2, 2026 National Stock Exchange of India Ltd. Exchange Plaza, Plot No. C/1, G Block, Bandra - Kurla Complex, Bandra (E), Mumbai - 400 051 Symbol: MUTHOOTFIN Department of Corporate Services BSE Limited P.J. Tower, Dalal Street, Mumbai - 400 001 Scrip Code: 533398 NSE IFSC Limited (NSE IX) Unit 1201, Brigade, International Financial Center, 12th Floor, Building No. 14-A, GIFT SEZ Gandhinagar, Gujarat 382 355 Dear Sir/Madam, Sub: Disclosure under Regulation 30, and other applicable regulations of the Securities and Exchange Board of India (Listing Obligations and Disclosure Requirements) Regulations, 2015, as amended (the “Listing Regulations”) Re: Search under the provisions Section 67 of CGST Act, 2017. Pursuant to Regulation 30 read with Schedule III and other applicable provisions of the Securities and Exchange Board of India (Listing Obligations and Disclosure Requirements) Regulations, 2015 (SEBI Regulations), we hereby inform you that a search and seizure operation was conducted by the GST Department at the Registered Office of the Company. The operation commenced on October 29, 2026, at around 11:00 IST and concluded on October 30, 2026, at around 21:30 IST. Company received the copy of the Search Mahasar on November 02, 2026, at around 11:00 IST. The Company has fully cooperated with the officials throughout the proceedings, providing all necessary clarifications and details as requested. We will continue to extend our support and furnish any further information required. We would like to emphasize that the Company’s business operations remained unaffected and continued as usual during this process. The Company has been consistently complying with the provisions of the SEBI (LODR) Regulations, 2015 and making requisite disclosures in a timely manner and will continue to do so in accordance with the applicable regulations. For Muthoot Finance Limited Rajesh A Company Secretary ICSI Membership No. FCS 7106","bodyFetched":true,"line":"GST department searched the registered office over 29–30 Oct; the company says it cooperated and operations were unaffected.","lineSource":"filing","eventTags":["gst search","indirect tax"]},{"id":"bde151b10537","symbol":"MUTHOOTFIN","company":"Muthoot Finance Ltd","date":"2026-11-02","at":"2026-11-02T12:00:00.000Z","timePrecision":"day","title":"Announcement under Regulation 30 (LODR)-Newspaper Publication","subject":"Newspaper Publication","note":null,"noteSource":null,"url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=fd7ec722-53fb-45c2-9654-1fe78f545e0d.pdf","source":"screener/bse","category":"unclassified","kind":"newspaper","baseScore":4,"readCost":3,"rule":"subject:newspaper\\s*(publication|adverti","confidence":0.9,"body":"Muthoot Finance Limited 662028, Muthoot Finance : ot Ref: SEC/MFL/SE/2026/6783 November 02, 2026 National Stock Exchange of India Limited Department of Corporate Services Exchange Plaza, BSE Limited, Plot No. C/1, G Block, P. J. Tower, Dalal Street, Bandra-Kurla Complex Mumbai - 400 001 Bandra (E),Mumbai - 400 051 Scrip Code: 533398 Symbol: MUTHOOTFIN NSE IFSC Limited (NSE IX) Unit 1201, Brigade, International Financial Center, 12th Floor, Building No. 14-A, GIFT SEZ Gandhinagar, Gujarat 382 355 Dear Sir/Madam, Sub: Newspaper Advertisement of Unaudited Financial Results for the Quarter and Half Year ended September 30, 2026 ‘We enclose herewith, a copy of the Newspaper Advertisements published on November 01, 2026, in Business Line (All India edition) and Metro Vaartha (All Kerala edition) in respect of the Unaudited Financial Results for the Quarter and Half year ended September 30, 2026. For Muthoot Finance Limited Rajesh A Company Secretary ICSI Membership No. FCS 7106 The Muthoot Group MUMBAI businessline.portfoli SUNDAY - NOVEMBER 1 - 2026 o Safe Investing - bl - 9 Managing costs for seniors TAKING COVER. Health insurance is necessary and expensive for seniors. Here are a few ways to manage the costs — Sai Prabhakar Yadaval bl. research bureau IRDAI - the insurance regulator, continues tostress on insurance for all. This includes even the elderly. But, managing the costs is a personal endeavour as un- derwriting and premium costs cannot be dictated by the regu- lator. While the space for seniors to access health insurance is im- proving, we highlight a few prac- tices to manage the high costs. This spans product choice, the riders and a few practices to im- prove the product efficiency. PRODUCT CHOICE Firstly, itis imperative tounder- stand that one can rarely overdo insurance for the elderly. Be it the number of products or the coverage - the wider and deeper it is, the better it is. Multiple products can be utilised for the same treatment’s cover, by pre- authorisation from all insurers and the hospital’s insurance sec- tion, andunderstanding the lim- itsand conditions of each policy. ‘The basic cover is the univer- sal cover - PM JAY (Ayushman Bharat Pradhan Mantri Jan Arogya Yojana). This govern- ment of India scheme covers all elderly people of 70+ years in a X5 lakh health insurance scheme. This scheme is not de- pendent on the financial status ofthe policyholder which is un- like the other sections of the same scheme which are inten- ded for theless privileged. All individuals of more than 70 years shouldbe under this in- surance cover, essentially for tworeasons. ‘This can be paired with one’s existing policies including cent- ral and state government schemes, and this policy does not face the PED (pre-existing disease) waiting period of three years aswell. With around 15,000 empan- elledhospitalsinthe scheme, ac- cessing the benefits should not beout of reach as well. ‘The second recommendation is a group cover where available, evenat acost. Parents or in-laws should be included in corporate policies which are provided as a perquisite to employees even if the policies are overlapping between children. Group policies also face no PED period and generally face lower scru- tiny compared to an individual policy at the time of claims. A health insurance policy for a 70- year-old costs between 70,000 to 1 lakhbased on the risk char- acteristics. If a corporate policy is comparable on costs or lower, the policy should be preferred onaccount of the waiting period improvements. Onthe other hand, ina family floater, it may be advisable to group the seniors of the family in a different product and the younger ones in a different one. The high-risk nature of seniors may impact the overall cost for everyone and should be con- sidered independently with cost comparisonin mind. RIDERS ‘While there are several riders or add-ons for seniors to consider: PED reduction, OPD inclusion, consumables cover and others, we refer to the o","bodyFetched":true},{"id":"c288c9aeb35a","symbol":"MUTHOOTFIN","company":"Muthoot Finance Ltd","date":"2026-11-02","at":"2026-11-02T12:00:00.000Z","timePrecision":"day","title":"Announcement under Regulation 30 (LODR)-Press Release / Media Release","subject":"Press Release / Media Release","note":"Q2/H1 FY27 results: PAT up 39%, MD changes, Muthoot Money merger approved.","noteSource":"screener.in","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=b352b257-615f-42e5-a428-6d26a7a7b3ca.pdf","source":"screener/bse","category":"press_release","kind":"press","baseScore":34,"readCost":10,"rule":"subject:order|contract|bagging|wins?|lau","confidence":0.9,"body":null,"bodyFetched":false},{"id":"482a083414bd","symbol":"MUTHOOTFIN","company":"Muthoot Finance Ltd","date":"2026-11-02","at":"2026-11-02T12:00:00.000Z","timePrecision":"day","title":"Announcement under Regulation 30 (LODR)-Investor Presentation","subject":"Investor Presentation","note":null,"noteSource":null,"url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=511c0d4e-8263-406d-918c-484e74f17299.pdf","source":"screener/bse","category":"results","kind":"results-deck","baseScore":42,"readCost":28,"rule":"subject:investor presentation|results pr","confidence":0.9,"body":null,"bodyFetched":false},{"id":"f08810851c61","symbol":"MUTHOOTFIN","company":"Muthoot F