clarification sought|rumou?r ver","confidence":0.9,"body":"Sun Pharmaceutical Industries Limited Sun House, Plot No. 201 B/1, Western Express Highway, Goregaon (E), Mumbai – 400 063, Maharashtra, INDIA. Tel.: (91-22) 4324 4324 Fax: (91-22) 4324 4343 Website: www.sunpharma.com Email: secretarial@sunpharma.com CIN: L24230GJ1993PLC019050 Registered Office: SPARC, Tandalja, Vadodara – 390 012, Gujarat, INDIA. Reaching People. Touching Lives. 02 November 2026 To BSE Limited Phiroze Jeejeebhoy Towers Dalal Street, Mumbai – 400 001 BSE Code: 524715 National Stock Exchange of India Limited Exchange Plaza, Bandra Kurla Complex Bandra (East), Mumbai – 400 051 NSE Code: SUNPHARMA Subject: Clarification regarding news report relating to the Company’s Assam facility Dear Sir/Madam, This is with reference to the communications received from the Stock Exchanges seeking clarification on the news report dated 30 October 2026 captioned “India orders Sun Pharma to halt eye-care drug production at plant after quality lapses” (“News Report”) and the movement in the price of the Company’s shares. In this regard, Sun Pharmaceutical Industries Limited (“Company”) submits as follows: The News Report relates to developments that occurred in August 2026 and does not concern any new event or development occurring on 30 October 2026. The matter was assessed at the relevant time and was not considered to warrant a disclosure under Regulation 30 of the SEBI Listing Regulations. As regards the share price movement, it may also be noted that the Company announced its financial results for the quarter and half year ended 30 September 2026 on 30 October 2026. The Company is not in a position to attribute the movement in its share price to the News Report or to any particular factor. The Company further confirms that it is not aware of any material event or information requiring disclosure under Regulation 30 that has not been disclosed to the Stock Exchanges and that could explain the aforesaid movement in the price of its shares. Thank you. For Sun Pharmaceutical Industries Limited (Anoop Deshpande) Company Secretary and Compliance Officer ICSI Membership No.: A23983","bodyFetched":true},{"id":"eb06339dc12c","symbol":"SUNPHARMA","company":"Sun Pharmaceutical Industries Ltd","date":"2026-11-02","at":"2026-11-02T12:00:00.000Z","timePrecision":"day","title":"Clarification Sought From Sun Pharmaceutical Industries Ltd","subject":"Clarification Sought From Sun Pharmaceutical Industries Ltd","note":"Exchange has sought clarification from Sun Pharmaceutical Industries Ltd on November 2, 2026, with reference to news appeared in https://www.thehindu.com/ dated October 30, 2026 quoting …","noteSource":"screener.in","url":"https://www.screener.in/company/id/3245/","source":"screener/bse","category":"litigation","kind":"clarification","baseScore":58,"readCost":22,"rule":"subject:clarification sought|rumou?r ver","confidence":0.9,"body":null,"bodyFetched":false},{"id":"66057839b86a","symbol":"AUBANK","company":"AU Small Finance Bank Ltd","date":"2026-11-02","at":"2026-11-02T12:00:00.000Z","timePrecision":"day","title":"Reply To Clarification Sought By Stock Exchanges","subject":"Reply To Clarification Sought By Stock Exchanges","note":"Bank reports potential data leak in vehicle-loan SaaS platform affecting about 28.5 lakh customers.","noteSource":"screener.in","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=7ab4c849-67d1-4cc7-b74d-dc5f8a34281a.pdf","source":"screener/bse","category":"litigation","kind":"clarification","baseScore":48,"readCost":22,"rule":"subject:clarification sought|rumou?r ver","confidence":0.9,"body":"investorrelations@aubank.in Ref. No.: AUSFB/SEC/2026-27/287 Date: November 02, 2026 To, National Stock Exchange of India Ltd. Exchange Plaza, C-1, Block G, Bandra Kurla Complex, Bandra (East), Mumbai 400051, Maharashtra. NSE Symbol: AUBANK BSE Limited Phiroze Jeejeebhoy Towers, Dalal Street, Mumbai 400001, Maharashtra. Scrip Code: 540611 Dear Sir/Madam, Sub: Reply to clarification sought by Stock Exchanges This is with reference to the clarification sought by the Stock Exchanges dated November 02, 2026 in relation to the media report titled “AU Bank probes potential data leak”. In this regard, we wish to clarify that the Bank became aware (on October 29, 2026) about a potential data leakage incident involving a third-party Software-as-a-Service (“SAAS”) platform. This platform, which is hosted and managed by a reputed global third-party vendor, is used for onboarding Bank’s vehicle loan customers and contains customers’ information obtained at the time of loan onboarding. Based on the preliminary findings so far, the incident may have resulted in data leakage of some of the Bank’s vehicle loan customers. The Bank is undertaking a detailed internal and external forensic investigation, with the help of leading cyber security firms, to ascertain the nature and extent of potential data leakage (there are ~28.5 lacs vehicle loan customers onboarded through this platform). The Bank’s other systems remain unaffected, and all services are operating normally. The incident does not have any impact on the Bank’s business operations, financial performance or business continuity. We hereby reaffirm to all stakeholders that customer protection continues to be our highest priority. The matter has been reported to regulatory authorities including the Reserve Bank of India and CERT-In in accordance with applicable regulatory requirements. The Bank continues to closely monitor the situation and will make further disclosures, if required, in accordance with applicable regulatory requirements. This is for your information and records. Thanking You, Yours faithfully, For AU SMALL FINANCE BANK LIMITED Manmohan Parnami Company Secretary and Compliance Officer Membership No.: F9999","bodyFetched":true,"line":"Possible data leak at a third-party SaaS platform used to onboard vehicle-loan customers (~28.5 lakh on it); forensic probe under way, core systems unaffected.","lineSource":"filing","eventTags":["data breach","cybersecurity","vendor risk"]},{"id":"6399b3748b5b","symbol":"AUBANK","company":"AU Small Finance Bank Ltd","date":"2026-11-02","at":"2026-11-02T12:00:00.000Z","timePrecision":"day","title":"Clarification sought from AU Small Finance Bank Ltd","subject":"Clarification sought from AU Small Finance Bank Ltd","note":"Exchange has sought clarification from AU Small Finance Bank Ltd with reference to the media report appearing on https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com dated November 02, 2026,(Link: https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/business/india-business/au-bank-probes-potential-data-leak/articleshow/135380899.cms) ....","noteSource":"screener.in","url":"https://www.screener.in/company/id/1274092/","source":"screener/bse","category":"litigation","kind":"clarification","baseScore":58,"readCost":22,"rule":"subject:clarification sought|rumou?r ver","confidence":0.9,"body":null,"bodyFetched":false,"line":"Exchanges ask AU Bank to clarify a media report on a potential data leak.","lineSource":"filing","eventTags":["data breach","cybersecurity"]},{"id":"7e29b4b797ab","symbol":"SUNPHARMA","company":"Sun Pharmaceutical Industries Ltd","date":"2026-11-02","at":"2026-11-02T12:00:00.000Z","timePrecision":"day","title":"Clarification Sought From Sun Pharmaceutical Industries Ltd","subject":"Clarification Sought From Sun Pharmaceutical Industries Ltd","note":"Exchange has sought clarification from Sun Pharmaceutical Industries Ltd on November 2, 2026, with reference to news appeared in https://www.thehindu.com/ dated October 30, 2026 quoting …","noteSource":"screener.in","url":"https://www.screener.in/company/id/3245/","source":"screener/bse","category":"litigation","kind":"clarification","baseScore":58,"readCost":22,"rule":"subject:clarification sought|rumou?r ver","confidence":0.9,"body":null,"bodyFetched":false},{"id":"7afcebfb74a0","symbol":"AUBANK","company":"AU Small Finance Bank Ltd",